<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gunzelin of Hagen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1185</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Gunzelin I of Schwerin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gunzelin of Hagen was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> nobleman and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-saxony">Duke of Saxony</a>. After Henry conquered the Obotrite lands, he made Gunzelin governor of Schwerin and in 1167 created the County of Schwerin for him. Gunzelin's descendants ruled the county in western Mecklenburg until 1358.</p></div>
